time_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01ALVNYjLVDz3KEfHFspt8m4", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53067, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01ALVNYjLVDz3KEfHFspt8m4", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 57214, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **Version chosen:** The latest deploy, v2.3.1, was unhealthy, with an error rate of 18%. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production.\n- **Rollback:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0 now. The service passes health checks and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery, and it paged the on-call engineer.\n\nThe release candidate for v2.3.1 (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy in staging but still went to production. The incident notes this, and it's worth checking how the release got past that before anyone tries v2.3.1 again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Gmp8d7xPLHQX9VngMEWWxp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Ncf1DDrkpUFnB1i1tABEDs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01UkpqKFUxkFn1UZ3spbnNE4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VfTxQPdKhK4yNjGSRK8wxs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01ALVNYjLVDz3KEfHFspt8m4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the deploy of checkout-api v2.3.1 to production (us-east, us-west, eu-west), the service failed health checks and its error rate reached 18%. v2.3.1 was rolled back in all regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, all three regions run v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. Next step: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **Version chosen:** The latest deploy, v2.3.1, was unhealthy, with an error rate of 18%. v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production.\n- **Rollback:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0 now. The service passes health checks and the error rate is down to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery, and it paged the on-call engineer.\n\nThe release candidate for v2.3.1 (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy in staging but still went to production. The incident notes this, and it's worth checking how the release got past that before anyone tries v2.3.1 again.", "type": "text"}]}]}